      "content": "i get that, but i'm pretty healthy and i've already checked my diet—i'm not eating much red meat or anything. it's just frustrating to feel this way. i honestly don't have the time to go through a whole doctor's appointment and wait weeks for bloodwork results right now. is there like a certain upper limit or an aggressive dose that people in the biohacking community use to jumpstart their ferritin levels? like what's a dose that's actually gonna move the needle?",
